---
// Adapted from Morphin smooth-expand-accordion (native details; no JavaScript).
import SectionHead from './SectionHead.astro';
---
<section id="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-h" class="section"><div class="wrap">
 <SectionHead id="faq-h" eyebrow="04 / FAQ" strong="Good to know." lead="A few details before your first conversation." />
 <div class="faq-list">
  <details name="faq"><summary class="focus-ring"><span class="faq-disc">01</span><span>Where do replies go?</span><span class="faq-plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="faq-body"><p>The omp model calls <code>glen_reply</code>. glen returns that reply to the calling agent. Later replies stay in <code>glen inbox</code>.</p></div></details>
  <details name="faq"><summary class="focus-ring"><span class="faq-disc">02</span><span>Sessions already open in omp</span><span class="faq-plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="faq-body"><p>Run <code>glen install-extension</code>, then restart the omp session. Live sessions use the extension; idle sessions use omp RPC.</p></div></details>
  <details name="faq"><summary class="focus-ring"><span class="faq-disc">03</span><span>Check your setup</span><span class="faq-plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="faq-body"><p><code>glen doctor</code> shows which omp glen found, its version, and the paths it will use.</p></div></details>
  <details name="faq"><summary class="focus-ring"><span class="faq-disc">04</span><span>Codex timeouts</span><span class="faq-plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="faq-body"><p>Give glen commands a timeout of at least 100 seconds, or use <code>glen send --wait 5s</code> and repeat <code>glen wait &lt;job&gt; --timeout 5s</code>. Only a non-empty <code>CODEX_SANDBOX</code> marks Codex's sandbox; run <code>glen send</code> with escalated permissions there. <code>CODEX_SANDBOX_NETWORK_DISABLED=1</code> alone allows sending, and a real permission failure returns exit 6 with a hint. On Linux, a Codex sandbox hides omp's session locks, so under either variable glen refuses to resume a session over RPC (exit 6); the live route through the extension still works.</p></div></details>
  <details name="faq"><summary class="focus-ring"><span class="faq-disc">05</span><span>Which omp?</span><span class="faq-plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="faq-body"><p>Tested with omp 18.14.0. glen never writes session files: it reads them and sends through omp, which owns the writing.</p></div></details>
 </div>
</div></section>
